title: Hörsing Moves
subtitle: The Security Police are sent into the Mansfeld copper district.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 3 and e21_kun_done = 1 and e21_march_started = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 9
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_march_started = 1;
Q.e21_lux_leads = (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') ? 1 : 0;
var lux_line = (Q.history_luxemburgist || 0) >= (Q.history_offensive || 0);
Q.e21_can_avoid = 0;
if (Q.e21_lux_leads == 1 && (lux_line || Q.e21_offensive_plan == 1)) { Q.e21_can_avoid = 1; }
if (Q.luxemburg_alive == 1 && Q.e21_offensive_plan != 3) { Q.e21_can_avoid = 1; }
if (Q.kapp_outcome == 3 && Q.e21_offensive_plan != 3) { Q.e21_can_avoid = 1; }
!}

= Hörsing Moves

On 16 March Otto Hörsing, the Social Democratic Oberpräsident of the province of Saxony, announces that the Security Police will occupy the Mansfeld copper district and the works around Merseburg. He speaks of thefts and wildcat strikes. Halle-Merseburg is the reddest district in Germany, and it is ours.

[? if e21_offensive_plan = 3 : Kun has his occasion. Nobody in the Zentrale asks whether the rest of the country is ready. ?][? if e21_offensive_plan = 2 : The strike committees we prepared in Central Germany are ready, and waiting for word from Berlin. ?][? if e21_offensive_plan = 1 : We sent Kun away. Now Hörsing has attacked first, and Kun's friends in Berlin say the decision has been made for us. ?][? if e21_offensive_plan = 0 : The Zentrale has made no plans, and has one night to decide. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg has written in the margin of the draft call to arms: "A party that rises because it is impatient will be beaten because it is alone." ?]

The police are due in Eisleben on 19 March. The miners are already talking about coming out.

- @rising: Call the workers to arms.
- @strike: Call a strike in defence of the district.
- @refuse: Protest, and do not take the bait.

@rising
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Answer the police with rifles and hope the country follows. Kun's plan.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e21_march_mode = 2;
Q.e21_ma_out = 40 + (Q.e21_offensive_plan == 2 ? 20 : 0) + (Q.ruhr_red_army == 2 ? 40 : 0);
// the call to arms says it plainly: whoever is not with us is against us
Q.e21_ma_rift = (Q.e21_offensive_plan == 3) ? 1 : 0;
RG.district('halle', {militancy: 15, repression: 10, guards: 1.5});
RG.startStrike('halle', true);
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
RG.comply(20);
RG.news('To arms: Mansfeld answers Hörsing\'s police with rifles', 3);
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}
go-to: begin

@strike
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Defend Mansfeld and Leuna with the strike, and ask for nothing else. Brandler's people want this.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids strikes and occupations led by the councils.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e21_march_mode = 1;
Q.e21_ma_out = 60 + (Q.e21_offensive_plan == 2 ? 30 : 0) + (Q.open_letter == 1 ? 20 : 0) + (Q.kapp_outcome == 3 ? 20 : 0);
Q.e21_ma_rift = 0;
RG.district('halle', {militancy: 10, repression: 6});
RG.startStrike('halle', true);
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.comply(10);
RG.news('General strike in Central Germany against the police occupation', 3);
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}
go-to: begin

@begin
on-arrival: {!
Q.crisis = 1;
Q.crisis_march = 1;
Q.crisis_time = 0;
Q.week = 1;
Q.crisis_name = 'The March Action';
Q.crisis_goal = 'Bring enough of Germany out that Berlin calls the police back, without setting worker against worker.';
Q.crisis_momentum = 50;
Q.crisis_momentum_label = 0;
Q.e21_ma_need = 330;
Q.e21_leuna = 0;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}

[? if e21_march_mode = 2 : On 17 March the Zentrale decides to answer force with force. The Rote Fahne of the next day calls the workers to arms: whoever is not with us is against us. On 21 March the Mansfeld miners down tools, and the first shots are fired near Eisleben. ?][? if e21_march_mode = 1 : The Zentrale calls a strike against the police occupation, and for nothing else. The call is printed beside an appeal to the social democratic and independent workers to join it. On 21 March the Mansfeld miners come out, and the Leuna works stop the next day. ?]

@refuse
subtitle: The district will be bitter and the Left will never forgive it. The party stays whole.
choose-if: e21_can_avoid = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Zentrale has committed itself to the offensive and cannot back down now.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_march_mode = 0;
Q.march_action = 0;
RG.district('halle', {repression: 15, loyalty: -10, militancy: -6});
if (Q.directive_offensive == 1) { RG.defy(); }
if (Q.comrade_hoelz != 4) { RG.arrest('hoelz', 0, {news: 'Max Hoelz arrested in Berlin under a false name', priority: 2}); }
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
Q.lean_offensive -= 2;
RG.ledger('The party refused Hörsing\'s provocation in March 1921, and there was no March Action.', 'e21_no_march');
!}

The Zentrale protests in the Landtag and the press, calls mass meetings and tells the district not to take up arms. The police enter Mansfeld on 19 March.

Max Hoelz, who answers to nobody, comes anyway with a few hundred men from the Vogtland. He robs banks and blows up a courthouse, and is hunted down within a fortnight.
